ence with evidence citing nonexistent files.\nfindings-and-improvements.md-524- \nfindings-and-improvements.md-523- When the LLM cites a path like `cluster-resources/pods/default/app-pod.json`, `matchChunkForEvidence` looks for it in the chunk index. If the path doesn't match any chunk (common because chunk IDs use fabricated paths — see 1.2), the evidence item is still included with `artifactType: undefined`. No confidence penalty, no filtering. A finding can have 100% confidence with evidence citing nonexistent files.\nfindings-and-improvements.md-524- \nfindings-and-improvements.md-525- Fix: after `convertAIFindings`, check each evidence item against the chunk index. If the path doesn't match any chunk's `artifactId`, either drop the evidence item or penalize the finding's confidence (-0.10 per ungrounded citation). If all evidence items are ungrounded, drop the entire finding.\nfindings-and-improvements.md-526- \nfindings-and-improvements.md:527: ### 7.2 AI confidence is unscored — LLM value taken at face value\nfindings-and-improvements.md-528- **Files:** `src/investigators/ai-investigator.ts`, `src/investigators/orchestrator.ts`\nfindings-and-improvements.md-529- \nfindings-and-improvements.md-530- The LLM returns `confidence: 1.0` and it's used directly. No adjustment for evidence grounding strength, hallucinated paths, thin evidence, or cross-source diversity. The heuristic pipeline has a multi-factor confidence model (verifier + hypothesis ranker). The AI pipeline has none.\nfindings-and-improvements.md-531- \nfindings-and-improvements.md-530- The LLM returns `confidence: 1.0` and it's used directly. No adjustment for evidence grounding strength, hallucinated paths, thin evidence, or cross-source diversity. The heuristic pipeline has a multi-factor confidence model (verifier + hypothesis ranker). The AI pipeline has none.\nfindings-and-improvements.md-531- \nfindings-and-improvements.md-532- Fix: apply a confidence scoring pass to AI findings after conversi