ltiple independent sources.\nREADME.md-529- \nREADME.md-530- **DiagnosticGraph.** A unified graph replaces two disconnected legacy graphs. It combines structural K8s edges (owner-refs, label-selectors, service-selectors), causal edges (from template matching and investigators), and temporal edges (log chunk ↔ event correlations, sequential event causality). Graph traversal for AI retrieval uses this richer edge set.\nREADME.md-526- **Differential diagnosis.** For each symptom, 3-5 competing root-cause hypotheses are generated from a declarative template registry and scored. The top finding includes an explicit comparison explaining why the runner-up was rejected.\nREADME.md-527- \nREADME.md-528- **Confidence quality, not just a number.** Every finding carries `confidenceQuality: strong | moderate | weak` alongside the numeric confidence. `81% (weak)` means the number could shift significantly with more bundle data; `100% (strong)` means it's well-grounded across multiple independent sources.\nREADME.md-529- \nREADME.md:530: **DiagnosticGraph.** A unified graph replaces two disconnected legacy graphs. It combines structural K8s edges (owner-refs, label-selectors, service-selectors), causal edges (from template matching and investigators), and temporal edges (log chunk ↔ event correlations, sequential event causality). Graph traversal for AI retrieval uses this richer edge set.\nREADME.md-531- \nREADME.md-532- **BM25 + Reciprocal Rank Fusion.** Lexical search uses proper BM25 (TF saturation k1=1.2, length normalisation b=0.75, IDF). Graph, lexical, and semantic results are merged via RRF (k=60).\nREADME.md-533- \nREADME.md-534- **Late chunking with TEI.** When TEI is running, each log chunk gets an embedding that encodes full-document context via token-level average pooling. A log error at line 3000 implicitly encodes `DB_HOST=db.internal` from line 12 because the transformer saw the entire document."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774104504147}}
